You are deploying a container app that must pull its image from a private ACR without embedding registry credentials as secrets:
```bicep
resource containerApp 'Microsoft.App/containerApps@2024-03-01' = {
  name: 'orders-api'
  location: location
  identity: {
    type: 'UserAssigned'
    userAssignedIdentities: {
      '${uami.id}': {}
    }
  }
  properties: {
    configuration: {
      registries: [
        {
          server: 'myregistry.azurecr.io'
          identity: uami.id
        }
      ]
    }
    template: {
      containers: [
        {
          name: 'orders-api'
          image: 'myregistry.azurecr.io/orders-api:1.0'
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
Deployment fails with an image pull authorization error. What is missing?

A Container App needs to reach an internal-only PostgreSQL server inside a peered VNET, and must not be reachable from the public internet at all — only from other services in the same Container Apps Environment and peered VNETs.
```bicep
resource env 'Microsoft.App/managedEnvironments@2024-03-01' = {
  name: 'orders-env'
  location: location
  properties: {
    vnetConfiguration: {
      infrastructureSubnetId: subnet.id
      internal: true
    }
  }
}
```
Which ingress configuration on the Container App correctly complements this environment setting for a fully internal-only app?

You define a KEDA-based scale rule for a Container App that should scale out based on the depth of an Azure Storage Queue:
```json
{
  "scale": {
    "minReplicas": 0,
    "maxReplicas": 10,
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "queue-scale-rule",
        "custom": {
          "type": "azure-queue",
          "metadata": {
            "queueName": "orders-queue",
            "queueLength": "5"
          },
          "auth": [
            {
              "secretRef": "storage-connection-string",
              "triggerParameter": "connection"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
The app never scales beyond 1 replica even though the queue has 50 messages. What is the most likely cause?

